  "notes": "The bridge between 90s neotraditional and 2000s adult-contemporary country — a clean soprano over an increasingly pop board. The drums follow the entry: \"verse on hats or cross-stick, chorus with full kit and tambourine; the uptempo cuts use a two-beat with the hat opening on 4. Snare tuned high and tight, low reverb after 2003,\" which is the beat-4 open hat plus a tight, high ghost velocity and a small fill count. The bass line is stated in two gears — \"root-fifth with walking pickups; 8ths under choruses, halves under verses\" — so the walking passing-tone set stays wide while root-following stays high. Harmony is the stated rotation set: I–V–vi–IV, I–IV–I–V and a vi–IV–I–V verse-into-chorus turn. Melody is \"mid-register verse with clear diction, chorus a fifth higher with sustained notes; ornament is minimal (no melisma),\" which is why the octave-jump probability is the lowest of the 90s female group here and the interval mix is step-dominant. The palette migrates \"to piano + electric + string pad by 2005; mandolin as a bright chorus layer,\" which is the counter's pad/answer split. ⚠ Confidence is medium, matching the research. The per-track readings are [LOW-CONF]. ⚠ The INFERRED parameters are the ghost velocities, the perc density and the counter ratio.",
